Phase 3 — Part 2: Load Balancing + Auto Scaling Architecture
Project Overview
This project demonstrates how to build a highly available, self‑healing, scalable cloud architecture using AWS Application Load Balancers (ALB), Target Groups, Launch Templates, Auto Scaling Groups (ASG), Scaling Policies, Health Checks, and Instance Refresh.
I performed hands‑on tasks including configuring load balancers, creating target groups, building launch templates, deploying Auto Scaling Groups, testing scaling events, and validating health checks.
This represents real production‑grade cloud engineering work.

